---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Privacy Policy | braininjurycalc.com';
const description = 'How braininjurycalc.com handles your data, including analytics, advertising cookies, the case-review form, and your rights under GDPR, CCPA, and other privacy laws.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p><em>Last updated: July 2026.</em></p>

  <p>braininjurycalc.com ("the Site") is operated by The Click Lab Agency LLC ("we," "us," "our"). This Privacy Policy describes what information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and what rights you have. We've written it in plain language because the brain injury content on this site reaches people in difficult circumstances, and clarity about data handling matters.</p>

  <h2>Summary</h2>
  <p>Short version: reading the calculator, guides, methodology page, or any other content on this Site does not require an account and does not send us your name, phone number, or email address. Calculator inputs are processed in your browser and are not transmitted to our servers. Separately, this Site offers an optional case-review form. If you fill it out and submit it, your name, phone number, email address, and case details are shared with one or more attorneys or their agents so they can evaluate your situation and potentially contact you &mdash; that's the whole point of the form, and it's covered in detail below. We use Google Analytics in a low-identifiability configuration to understand traffic patterns and display ads served by Google AdSense, which uses cookies to show relevant ads.</p>

  <h2>1. Information you provide directly</h2>
  <p><strong>The calculator.</strong> The calculator on this Site is client-side. When you enter injury details, pre-injury income, age, and state to compute an estimated recovery range, those values are processed in your browser and are not transmitted to our servers. We do not log calculator inputs.</p>
  <p><strong>The case-review form.</strong> This Site includes an optional "Talk to a Brain Injury attorney" form. If you fill it out, we collect your first and last name, email address, phone number, ZIP code, approximate incident date, a description of what happened, the timestamp you gave consent, and the exact consent text you agreed to. Submitting this form is entirely optional and is never required to use the calculator, read any guide, or access any other part of the Site.</p>
  <p>If you choose to email us instead, the contents of your email (sender address, body, and any attachments) are received by our email provider and retained for as long as needed to handle the conversation. We don't sell that information, and we don't share it with attorneys unless you separately use the case-review form.</p>

  <h2>2. How your case-review information is shared</h2>
  <p>If you submit the case-review form, your name, phone number, email address, and case details are shared with one or more attorneys or their agents licensed to practice in your jurisdiction, so they can evaluate your situation and contact you about it. The Click Lab Agency LLC, which operates braininjurycalc.com, is not a law firm, does not provide legal advice, and does not vet, endorse, or guarantee the attorneys in this network. Submitting the form does not create an attorney-client relationship with The Click Lab Agency LLC or with any attorney until and unless that attorney separately agrees to represent you. The Click Lab Agency LLC may be compensated for these referrals.</p>
  <p>By submitting the form, you separately consent to be contacted by phone, text, and email &mdash; including by automated dialing technology &mdash; by The Click Lab Agency LLC and the attorneys or agents your information is shared with. That consent is not required to use any other part of this site, and you can decline it by not submitting the form.</p>

  <h2>3. Information collected automatically</h2>
  <p>Like virtually all modern websites, our hosting provider's edge layer and our analytics provider receive some automatically-transmitted data from every visit. This typically includes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Your IP address (used to determine approximate location for analytics, discarded after standard retention).</li>
    <li>Browser type and version, operating system, device type, and screen resolution.</li>
    <li>Referrer URL (the page you came from, if any).</li>
    <li>The pages you visit on this Site and how long you spend on each.</li>
    <li>Generic events like page-loads and outbound link clicks.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Cookies</h2>
  <p>This Site uses a small number of cookies, split by purpose:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Strictly necessary cookies</strong> &mdash; storing privacy preferences themselves.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics cookies</strong> &mdash; Google Analytics cookies that distinguish your session from other visitors'.</li>
    <li><strong>Advertising cookies</strong> &mdash; Google AdSense cookies for ad personalization. You can opt out via Google's ad settings (see Section 6).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>5. Google Analytics</h2>
  <p>We use Google Analytics 4 in a default-privacy configuration: IP addresses are truncated before storage, ad personalization signals are disabled where possible, and we don't merge GA data with personally identifying user profiles. Google's data handling for Analytics is described at <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>. To opt out of GA entirely, install Google's browser opt-out: <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout</a>.</p>

  <h2>6. Google AdSense advertising</h2>
  <p>This Site displays ads from Google AdSense (publisher ID pub-6434377544325972). When AdSense renders an ad, Google uses cookies to (a) prevent fraudulent ad clicks, (b) frequency-cap which ads you see, and (c) optionally personalize the ads. You can review and adjust Google's ad personalization settings at <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">adssettings.google.com</a> or opt out of third-party ad personalization via <a href="https://aboutads.info" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">aboutads.info</a> or (EU/UK) <a href="https://youronlinechoices.eu" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">youronlinechoices.eu</a>.</p>
  <p>Opting out of personalized advertising does not stop ads from appearing; it stops them being matched to your inferred interests.</p>

  <h2>7. Other third parties</h2>
  <p>Browsing the calculator, guides, or methodology page does not result in your data being sold or shared with third parties. If you submit the case-review form, Section 2 above describes exactly what is shared with attorneys and why. Beyond Google Analytics, Google AdSense, and (only if you submit the case-review form) the attorney network described in Section 2, the only third parties that may see data about your visit are our hosting provider's CDN and any third-party site you click through to (e.g., state agency pages, court opinions linked from guides).</p>

  <h2>8. Opt-out</h2>
  <p>The simplest opt-out is not to submit the case-review form. Browsing the rest of the Site never shares your name, phone number, or email address with anyone.</p>
  <p>If you've already submitted the form and want to opt out of further contact or request deletion, email <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a> with the subject line <strong>[OPT-OUT]</strong>, or visit <a href="https://theclicklab.agency/optout" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">theclicklab.agency/optout</a>.</p>

  <h2>9. Your rights under GDPR (EEA, UK)</h2>
  <p>If you're in the EEA or UK, the GDPR gives you several rights: access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability, and objection. To exercise these, email <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>. We'll respond within 30 days. Our legal basis for processing is generally (a) consent &mdash; for non-essential cookies, and for any information you submit through the case-review form, which we process only because you have affirmatively opted in and which you may withdraw at any time via the opt-out channels in Section 8 &mdash; and (b) our legitimate interest in operating, securing, and improving the Site.</p>

  <h2>10. Your rights under CCPA / CPRA (California)</h2>
  <p>California residents have the right to know what personal information we collect, to delete personal information, to opt out of "sale" or "sharing" of personal information, and to non-discrimination for exercising any of these rights. Two things count as a "sale" or "sharing" of personal information under CCPA/CPRA: the use of advertising cookies (see Section 6), and, if you submit the case-review form, the disclosure of your information to attorneys in exchange for compensation (see Section 2). You can opt out of either via the channels in Section 6 or Section 8, respectively. Simply browsing this Site anonymously &mdash; without submitting the case-review form &mdash; is never sold or shared. To exercise other CCPA rights, contact <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>.</p>

  <h2>11. Do Not Track</h2>
  <p>We honor DNT signals to the extent that, when DNT is on, we disable advertising personalization. We don't disable analytics on DNT alone. For analytics-off entirely, use the GA opt-out plugin.</p>

  <h2>12. Children's privacy (COPPA)</h2>
  <p>This Site is intended for adults dealing with brain injury matters. We don't knowingly collect information from children under 13, including through the case-review form. If you believe we have, contact us at <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a> and we'll delete it.</p>

  <h2>13. Security</h2>
  <p>HTTPS on all pages, no user accounts, limited access to admin accounts and to case-review submissions. Standard practices for a static informational site that also operates a disclosed lead-intake form.</p>

  <h2>14. International transfers</h2>
  <p>Our hosting provider, Google's services, and (if you submit the case-review form) the attorneys or agents your information is shared with may process data outside your country (typically the United States). We rely on standard contractual clauses where required.</p>

  <h2>15. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We update this policy as needed. When we do, we update the "Last updated" date at the top. Material changes will be announced on the home page. Continued use of the Site after a change indicates acceptance.</p>

  <h2>16. Contact</h2>
  <p>Privacy questions, including opt-out requests: <a href="mailto:hey@theclicklab.agency">hey@theclicklab.agency</a>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
